{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "7241460",
      "title": "Why Would You Use Angular?",
      "lectureOrder": 3,
      "videoOrder": 3,
      "sourceHash": "17f6930779b295dadcf99a90ad139cf126c128aae8708a7b85f6479ac4de9fee",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.3,
          "end": 4.632,
          "en": "So now that you know what Angular is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.632,
          "end": 6.54,
          "en": "a valid question, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.54,
          "end": 9.66,
          "en": "would be why you would use Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.66,
          "end": 14.34,
          "en": "Why would you use a framework like Angular in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.34,
          "end": 18.33,
          "en": "instead of just using just JavaScript?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.33,
          "end": 22.83,
          "en": "And especially for pretty trivial web applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.83,
          "end": 25.26,
          "en": "and web user interfaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.26,
          "end": 30.21,
          "en": "you indeed might not need a solution like Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.21,
          "end": 34.38,
          "en": "But frameworks like Angular do really shine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.38,
          "end": 37.38,
          "en": "as your applications become more complex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.38,
          "end": 40.312,
          "en": "because they simplify the process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.312,
          "end": 45.312,
          "en": "of building complex, highly interactive web user interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 49.8,
          "en": "And Angular does simplify this process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.8,
          "end": 54.54,
          "en": "by giving you many useful features, and rules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 54.54,
          "end": 57.42,
          "en": "and concepts you should apply when using it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 57.42,
          "end": 58.77,
          "en": "But most importantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.77,
          "end": 63.77,
          "en": "because of four main things it brings to the table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 63.78,
          "end": 66.3,
          "en": "And the first one is that with Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.3,
          "end": 70.74,
          "en": "you can write declarative code instead of imperative code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.74,
          "end": 73.83,
          "en": "as you do it with Vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.83,
          "end": 77.64,
          "en": "And this simply means that with Vanilla JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 82.64,
          "en": "you have to step by step, write every single instruction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 82.77,
          "end": 85.44,
          "en": "that should be executed by the browser so that you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 85.44,
          "end": 89.22,
          "en": "for example, want to reach out to some DOM element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 89.22,
          "end": 91.38,
          "en": "that you then have certain conditions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 91.38,
          "end": 92.72999999999999,
          "en": "that should be validated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.72999999999999,
          "end": 95.85,
          "en": "and that then depending on which condition is met",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.85,
          "end": 100.28999999999999,
          "en": "or what happened, you want to change something in the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.28999999999999,
          "end": 103.02000000000001,
          "en": "You have to all write it down explicitly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.02000000000001,
          "end": 107.25,
          "en": "and give the browser those step by step instructions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 107.25,
          "end": 110.49000000000001,
          "en": "With frameworks like Angular that changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 110.49000000000001,
          "end": 113.03999999999999,
          "en": "There you instead write declarative code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 113.03999999999999,
          "end": 118.03999999999999,
          "en": "which means you define the target state or states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.08,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "So in the end, some markup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 122.82,
          "en": "that contains special instructions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 122.82,
          "end": 125.1,
          "en": "that are unlocked by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 125.1,
          "end": 129.15,
          "en": "so that would not work with just Vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.15,
          "end": 131.37,
          "en": "The browser wouldn't understand them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.37,
          "end": 134.07,
          "en": "but they are unlocked by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.07,
          "end": 138.69,
          "en": "and they allow you to define different target states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.69,
          "end": 141.18,
          "en": "and then you can also write some logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.18,
          "end": 144.222,
          "en": "that makes sure that those states get activated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.222,
          "end": 147.51,
          "en": "or deactivated depending on the occurrence",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.51,
          "end": 149.73,
          "en": "of certain events and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.73,
          "end": 152.25,
          "en": "But it's then Angular's job",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.25,
          "end": 155.67000000000002,
          "en": "to figure out which steps must be taken",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.67000000000002,
          "end": 159.3,
          "en": "to update the visible user interface accordingly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.3,
          "end": 163.89,
          "en": "so that those target states are reflected on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.89,
          "end": 166.62,
          "en": "That's what declarative code means.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.62,
          "end": 170.57999999999998,
          "en": "You don't have to manually reach out to those DOM elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.57999999999998,
          "end": 172.05,
          "en": "or anything like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.05,
          "end": 175.5,
          "en": "instead you write declarative code in your markup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.5,
          "end": 178.29,
          "en": "and Angular does the heavy lifting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.29,
          "end": 181.29,
          "en": "In addition, Angular also allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.29,
          "end": 183.966,
          "en": "to easily separate concerns",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.966,
          "end": 187.68,
          "en": "by embracing a concept called Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.68,
          "end": 190.183,
          "en": "When working with Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.183,
          "end": 193.59,
          "en": "you built a lot of so-called Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.59,
          "end": 197.61,
          "en": "which essentially are custom HTML elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.61,
          "end": 198.622,
          "en": "you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.622,
          "end": 201.18,
          "en": "a combination of markups, styling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.18,
          "end": 203.85,
          "en": "and logic, which you can then use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.85,
          "end": 207.27,
          "en": "to build the overall user interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.27,
          "end": 210.78,
          "en": "And therefore you can break complex user interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.78,
          "end": 215.78,
          "en": "up into simpler parts and then compose them together again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.97,
          "end": 217.62,
          "en": "But by breaking everything up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.62,
          "end": 220.05,
          "en": "into those simpler building blocks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.05,
          "end": 222.57,
          "en": "you can also break up complex problems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.57,
          "end": 227.07,
          "en": "and reduce the complexity of the overall web user interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 227.07,
          "end": 230.824,
          "en": "and therefore simplify the development process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 230.824,
          "end": 234.36,
          "en": "In addition, of course, since you do work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 234.36,
          "end": 236.22,
          "en": "with multiple such Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.22,
          "end": 237.78,
          "en": "you also make it easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.78,
          "end": 240.78,
          "en": "to work on complex applications in a team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 240.78,
          "end": 244.92,
          "en": "since it's easier to assign different team members",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.92,
          "end": 246.9,
          "en": "to different parts of the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.9,
          "end": 249.903,
          "en": "since you have those different Components anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.89,
          "end": 255.89,
          "en": "Another crucial feature Angular brings to the table",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 255.96,
          "end": 258.96,
          "en": "is that it embraces some, not all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.96,
          "end": 262.5,
          "en": "but some object oriented programming concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.5,
          "end": 264.24,
          "en": "and principles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.24,
          "end": 268.5,
          "en": "Now, you don't have to know object oriented programming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.5,
          "end": 270.57,
          "en": "or be an expert there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.57,
          "end": 272.43,
          "en": "You will learn everything you need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 272.43,
          "end": 274.35,
          "en": "to know throughout this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.35,
          "end": 278.174,
          "en": "but by giving you features like dependency injection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 278.174,
          "end": 281.748,
          "en": "or classes, Angular gives you tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 281.748,
          "end": 286.142,
          "en": "that can make it a bit easier to build complex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 286.142,
          "end": 290.19,
          "en": "and scalable web applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 290.19,
          "end": 293.298,
          "en": "And then there's one last tool,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 293.298,
          "end": 296.282,
          "en": "one last thing Angular gives you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 296.282,
          "end": 299.07,
          "en": "which can also help with the development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 299.07,
          "end": 303.24,
          "en": "of possibly complex web user interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 303.24,
          "end": 305.76,
          "en": "And that would be TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 305.76,
          "end": 310.59,
          "en": "Angular uses TypeScript, not Vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 310.59,
          "end": 312.75,
          "en": "So as an Angular developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 312.75,
          "end": 317.193,
          "en": "you actually write TypeScript code, not JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 318.24,
          "end": 321.24,
          "en": "Now, the good news is you don't need to know TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 321.24,
          "end": 322.32,
          "en": "for this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 322.32,
          "end": 324.84,
          "en": "You'll learn it all along the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 324.84,
          "end": 328.71,
          "en": "because in the end, TypeScript just is JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 328.71,
          "end": 332.82,
          "en": "with strict and strong typing added to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 332.82,
          "end": 334.56,
          "en": "so that you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 334.56,
          "end": 337.31,
          "en": "can't easily switch the type of a value or,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 337.31,
          "end": 340.645,
          "en": "and that's the advantage of using TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 340.645,
          "end": 345.27,
          "en": "that it's easier to catch simple errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 345.27,
          "end": 347.52,
          "en": "where you might be working with a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 347.52,
          "end": 349.967,
          "en": "that's not necessarily set yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 349.967,
          "end": 353.67,
          "en": "or where you might be passing the wrong kind of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 353.67,
          "end": 356.55,
          "en": "to a certain function or method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 356.55,
          "end": 358.59000000000003,
          "en": "And without TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 358.59000000000003,
          "end": 361.492,
          "en": "those errors would be undetected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 361.492,
          "end": 365.94,
          "en": "and would then possibly only surface at runtime",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 365.94,
          "end": 367.74,
          "en": "when your application crashes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 367.74,
          "end": 370.17,
          "en": "or behaves incorrectly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 370.17,
          "end": 372.12,
          "en": "with the usage of TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 372.12,
          "end": 374.49,
          "en": "you can instead catch them early on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 374.49,
          "end": 376.68,
          "en": "during the development process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 376.68,
          "end": 379.32,
          "en": "hence leading to better code quality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 379.32,
          "end": 382.95,
          "en": "and possibly less errors in your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 382.95,
          "end": 386.55,
          "en": "And that's why Angular does embrace TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 386.55,
          "end": 388.617,
          "en": "and why as a Angular developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 388.617,
          "end": 391.41,
          "en": "you have to work with TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 391.41,
          "end": 394.38,
          "en": "But as mentioned, that's not something to worry about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 394.38,
          "end": 397.5,
          "en": "You'll learn it all step by step throughout this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 397.5,
          "end": 399.603,
          "en": "as you are learning Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
